{% comment %}
  snippets/labor-day-sale-note.liquid

  Price-adjacent sale note on eligible PDPs, keyed to ACTUAL discount eligibility
  (collection membership), not the product title. Replaces the previous
  title-string block in the four product templates (main-product, -comb,
  -variants, -home-gym-packages).

  Accepts:
    product         (Product)  required
    hide_on_mobile  (boolean)  optional. Pass true on the desktop-layout copy so it
                               does not also render on mobile (the mobile-layout copy
                               is rendered without it and is the one shown on phones).

  ELIGIBILITY: mirrors each discount collection's own smart-collection rules, read from
  non-truncating product fields (vendor / type / tags / title). It deliberately does NOT
  use product.collections, which truncates when a product is in more than ~20 collections
  (so the eligible collection could be missed), and it does NOT depend on the collection
  being published to the Online Store. The automatic discounts still target the
  collections by ID, so this note matches exactly which products get discounted.
    French Fitness 10% (collection 519462814012, all must be true):
      vendor == 'French Fitness' AND type != 'Product (Hidden)' AND no 'july4-exclude' tag
    Remanufactured 5% (collection 512180715836, all must be true):
      title contains 'Remanufactured' AND type == 'Product Index'

  DISPLAY: renders as a compact sale card, not a free-text paragraph. The payoff line
  (percentage + discounted price) is computed in Liquid from product.price rather than
  read from settings.sale_promo_ff / settings.sale_promo_reman, so it always matches the
  real discount. Those two settings still gate the card per branch (blank = hidden) and
  the end date shown comes from settings.laborday_end, so a future sale only needs the
  theme settings updated - no code edit.
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign in_ff = false
  assign in_reman = false

  if product.vendor == 'French Fitness' and product.type != 'Product (Hidden)'
    unless product.tags contains 'july4-exclude'
      assign in_ff = true
    endunless
  endif

  if product.type == 'Product Index' and product.title contains 'Remanufactured'
    assign in_reman = true
  endif

  comment
    campaign_kind drives which payoff line renders below. The settings.sale_promo_ff /
    settings.sale_promo_reman text fields are no longer displayed verbatim - the payoff
    line is computed from product.price - but a blank field still acts as a per-branch
    kill switch, same as before, so merchants can turn a branch off without a code edit.
  endcomment
  assign campaign_kind = ''
  if in_ff and settings.sale_promo_ff != blank
    assign campaign_kind = 'ff'
  elsif in_reman and settings.sale_promo_reman != blank
    assign campaign_kind = 'reman'
  endif
-%}
{%- comment -%} Date window (store timezone). Theme editor and force_preview both bypass it. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign now_s = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0 -%}
{%- assign start_s = settings.laborday_start | date: '%s' | plus: 0 -%}
{%- assign end_s = settings.laborday_end | date: '%s' | plus: 0 -%}
{%- assign in_window = false -%}
{%- if settings.laborday_force_preview or request.design_mode -%}
  {%- assign in_window = true -%}
{%- elsif start_s > 0 and end_s > 0 and now_s >= start_s and now_s < end_s -%}
  {%- assign in_window = true -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if campaign_kind != '' and in_window -%}
  <div class="campaign-sale-container{% if hide_on_mobile %} hide-on-mobile{% endif %}">
    <div class="labor-day-sale-card">
      <span class="labor-day-sale-card__badge">Labor day sale</span>
      {%- if campaign_kind == 'ff' -%}
        <p class="labor-day-sale-card__payoff">10% off — {{ product.price | times: 0.9 | money }} in cart</p>
      {%- elsif campaign_kind == 'reman' -%}
        <p class="labor-day-sale-card__payoff">5% off — {{ product.price | times: 0.95 | money }} in cart</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      <p class="labor-day-sale-card__meta">Applied automatically at checkout · Ends {{ settings.laborday_end | date: "%b. %-d" }}</p>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
